From 6d9deda0d20ef498a91720ee629e929168c6bdc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:35:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Invalidate role cache when expiring memberships revive

Federated users' expiring group memberships count towards their
effective role assignments only while they are valid, which depends on
the identity provider's authorization_ttl. Two changes make an existing
membership valid again without adding a new one, and neither
invalidated the computed role assignments cache:

- setting or changing authorization_ttl on the identity provider;
- a federated login that refreshes a membership that had expired.

A user who tried to create an application credential before the TTL was
set kept getting "Could not find role assignment" until the cache
expired ([cache] expiration_time, 600 seconds by default), although the
membership was already valid.

Invalidate the computed assignments region when an identity provider's
authorization_ttl changes, and report a refresh that turns an expired
membership into a valid one as a membership change, so that
shadow_federated_user invalidates the user's cached assignments as it
does for a new membership. A refresh without a TTL leaves the
membership expired and is still no change.

Related-Bug: #2119031
Signed-off-by: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
---
